51A.
Fundamental duties.-It shall be the duty of every citizen of India---
(a)
to abide by the Constitution and respect its ideals and institutions, the National Flag and the National Anthem;
(b)
to cherish and follow the noble ideals which inspired our national struggle for freedom;
(c)
to uphold and protect the sovereignty, unity and integrity of India;
Page 6/19

THE CONSTITUTION (FORTY-SECOND AMENDMENT) ACT, 1976
(d)
to defend the country and render national service when called upon to do so;
(e)
to promote harmony and the sprit of common brotherhood amongst all the people of India transcending religious,
linguistic and regional or sectional diversities; to renounce practices derogatory to the dignity of women;
(f)
to value and preserve the rich heritage of our composite culture;
(g)
to protect and improve the natural environment including forests, lakes, rivers and wild life, and to have compassion for
living creatures;
(h)
to develop the scientific temper, humanism and the sprit of inquiry and reform;
(i)
to safeguard public property and to abjure violence;
(j)
to strive towards excellence in all spheres of individual and collective activity so that the nation constantly rises to higher
levels of endeavour and achievement.".
